WHY THIS SOURCE IS PUBLIC

MoxSpeak asks macOS for Accessibility access so it can read the text you have
selected. That is a serious permission to grant a program, and you should not
have to take anyone's word for what it does with it. The source is published so
that you, or anyone you trust, can read exactly what is sent off your machine
and what is not. It is not published as an invitation to redistribute it.

WHAT YOU MAY DO

- Read, study and audit this source code, for any purpose.
- Build it and run your own build on machines you own or control.
- Modify it for your own use.
- Submit changes back to the project.
- Quote it, in whole or in part, in reviews, articles, security write-ups and
  teaching materials.

WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO, without prior written permission from the copyright holder

- Redistribute this software, or any work derived from it, in source or binary
  form, whether free of charge or not.
- Publish, host, sell, sublicense or offer it as a service.
- Remove or alter this notice, the copyright notices, or the third-party
